# 🎯 Objective
Just like how after a crime is committed, little bits and pieces of evidence are always left behind by the culprit—from something as small as facial hair to bigger things like footprints left while leaving the scene—no matter how much is removed or cleaned to hide evidence, there will always be that one bit of evidence that leads investigators to the culprit. 

With that being said, the digital world is also like a crime scene that keeps footprints of all your actions, even if an attempt to cover it up was made. Digital Forensics helps us uncover all these bits of evidence to reveal information essential to investigations.

